# Build context is frontend/ (the bun workspace root) — docker-compose.yml's
# `context: ./frontend`, the CI job and the Dockerfile's own header comment all
# build with `-f apps/web/Dockerfile` from here. Docker reads .dockerignore ONLY at
# the root of the context, and patterns without `**/` only match at that root — so
# an ignore file inside apps/web/ (as this used to be) is never read, and local
# build output leaked into the image: a stale or half-written `.next/dev/types` from
# `next dev` fails `next build`'s type check ("Declaration or statement expected").

# Dependencies come from the `deps` stage, and Next's own output is rebuilt.
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/.turbo

**/.git
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# Local secrets stay out of the context — the builder stage does `COPY . .`, so
# anything not excluded here ends up in the image. The exceptions: the example file,
# and apps/web/.env.local, which only holds public build-time values
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_*, the OpenAPI URL) and is where a local `docker compose build`
# gets NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID from when the root .env doesn't set it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.local
!**/.env.local.example

# Not `*.md`: the fairy tales the "Казки" game reads at runtime are
# public/static/stories/*/story.md and must reach the image.
